  "prompts": {
    "image": "CLOSE TWO-SHOT, from waist upward, seated faces large in the upper third. EXACT crop and camera of input 1 with people placed as input 2; NO feet or full-body framing. Use case: sketch-to-render / photorealistic-natural. Create ONE final live-action film still, 16:9, ideally 1920x1080. Input 1 is a WORKING BLENDER RENDER, strictly a camera, spatial layout, scale and composition reference, NOT the final visual style. Input 2 is a SMALL PERSPECTIVE/BLOCKING GUIDE of the same camera: its converging lines explain real spatial directions and its primitive figures mark human placement. Do not reproduce the guide, linework, captions, faceted bodies, plastic surfaces or crude geometry. Rebuild the visible scene as a convincing photographed physical place while retaining the prescribed viewpoint, major dimensions, openings, object positions and framing. Improve natural material variation, construction details, contact shadows and realistic light; do not redesign the layout or invent different architecture. No game-engine look, no illustration, no split panels, no watermark. Early-1990s provincial Polish atmosphere, understated cinematic realism and restrained film grain, no modern products. Input 3 is the exact production identity and wardrobe reference: Dariusz is the chubby red-brown wavy-haired boy with rectangular dark glasses on the LEFT of that reference; Owczar is the slim dark-blond boy in the burgundy track jacket on its RIGHT. Both are 13–14, clean-shaven. Preserve their specific faces, hair, age, body shape and clothing. Owczar has TWO cream stripes on each sleeve, ivory T-shirt, loose blue jeans and worn pale canvas trainers. Dariusz has an open grey-blue plaid overshirt, grey/navy striped T-shirt, dark loose jeans and dark worn trainers. Their positions in the final shot are dictated by the shot instructions, not by the identity reference layout. Replace all visible primitive stand-ins with anatomically natural boys, and insert the boys where requested even if the clean render is empty. No adult beard, no extra people. SHOT ACTION AND COMPOSITION: Both boys seated side by side on the steps, Dariusz screen left, Owczar screen right. Each holds his own opened small paper sachet. One hand with a small pinch of powder poised near the mouth, anticipating a sour taste; natural subtle amusement, not exaggerated faces. No drinking glasses. Soft urban overcast daylight, believable worn materials and subtle dirt without theatrical decay. Keep the same natural atmosphere across the street and shop sequence.  Input 4 specifies only the exact PAPER SACHET artwork and lettering; this is a palm-sized 6 by 9 cm paper packet, not a box. The printed glass is an illustration on the packet, never an actual glass in the scene. Preserve the orange and green print.  Input 5 is the approved later ending at the SAME steps, only for exact identities, wall finish and paper packets. Do not copy its full-body composition or shoulder-embrace action. In this earlier shot BOTH arms are free to handle the sachets and powder. Each boy has ONE packet in one hand and a small pinch of powder in the other near his mouth. ",
    "endFrameDescription": "Dariusz obejmuje Owczara ramieniem po pocieszeniu go, że kiedyś na pewno wygra. Owczar odzyskał humor; wspólny uśmiech wynika z koleżeńskiego wsparcia. Szerszy kadr z final-schodki, te same dwie saszetki.",
    "animation": "0.0–1.5s: Both boys taste the powder already pinched in their right hands and lower those hands. Owczar on screen right lets his gaze drop, shoulders slightly slumped. 1.5–3.5s: Each transfers his sachet from left to right hand. Dariusz on screen left turns toward Owczar with a warm, reassuring expression and a small confident nod. 3.5–6.0s: Dariusz gently rests his free left arm around Owczar shoulders. Owczar looks toward him, relaxes and smiles; their shared relieved smiles reach the supplied End Frame. Camera: continuous smooth pull-back to the End Frame composition. @Image1 fixes both existing boys identities only; preserve clothing, daylight and setting from Start/End. @Image2 fixes the existing sachets and lettering. Keep both seated. No mocking gestures, cuts, dissolves, teleportation, new people, duplicate packets, facial morphing or extra limbs."
